  "_comment": "Landing on a slope (SC-2a, 3. 10. 2026): the ship comes down on its own (lift -0.6 held) over ground of a given slope and stands on its three pads. space.SlopeSpot <min> <max> <yaw> moves it over the nearest such ground, the nose yaw degrees right of straight uphill. The last pair is too steep: the ship must not land (TOO STEEP) and slides on its gear, the hull out of the ground. Run: .\\Tools\\Shots.ps1 -Preset landing_slope -Editor",
